{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "intro",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🔬 Feature Ablation Analysis: What Features Actually Help?\n",
    "\n",
    "**A systematic study of feature importance and contribution in PS S6E2**\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook investigates which of the **18 engineered features** actually contributed to model performance through:\n",
    "- Feature ablation experiments (adding features incrementally)\n",
    "- SHAP-based feature importance rankings\n",
    "- Correlation analysis between features\n",
    "- Performance comparison across feature sets\n",
    "\n",
    "**Surprising Finding:** While engineered features helped LB (+0.00031), they actually **hurt OOF** (-0.00013). This notebook explores why."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "imports",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from catboost import CatBoostClassifier, Pool\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\n",
    "import shap\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_style('whitegrid')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (14, 6)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Environment detection\n",
    "nb_dir = Path.cwd()\n",
    "if Path('/kaggle/input').exists():\n",
    "    DATA_DIR = Path('/kaggle/input/playground-series-s6e2')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    if nb_dir.name == 'notebooks':\n",
    "        root = nb_dir.parent\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        root = nb_dir\n",
    "    DATA_DIR = root / 'data'\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Data directory: {DATA_DIR}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Exists: {DATA_DIR.exists()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "load-data",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📊 Load Data and Define Feature Sets\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll compare 4 feature sets:\n",
    "1. **Raw 13 features** - Original competition features\n",
    "2. **+ Expert features** - Medical domain knowledge (5 features)\n",
    "3. **+ Target encoding** - Categorical encoding (not used in final model)\n",
    "4. **+ Domain + original stats** - Additional domain features + original dataset statistics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "load-and-encode",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load data\n",
    "train = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / 'train.csv')\n",
    "test = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / 'test.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Encode target\n",
    "label_map = {'Presence': 1, 'Absence': 0}\n",
    "train['target'] = train['Heart Disease'].map(label_map)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Original 13 features\n",
    "RAW_FEATURES = [\n",
    "    'Age', 'Sex', 'Chest pain type', 'BP', 'Cholesterol', 'FBS over 120',\n",
    "    'EKG results', 'Max HR', 'Exercise angina', 'ST depression',\n",
    "    'Slope of ST', 'Number of vessels fluro', 'Thallium'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "NUMS = ['Age', 'BP', 'Cholesterol', 'Max HR', 'ST depression', 'Number of vessels fluro']\n",
    "CATS = ['Sex', 'Chest pain type', 'FBS over 120', 'EKG results', 'Exercise angina', 'Slope of ST', 'Thallium']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Train: {train.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test: {test.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Raw features: {len(RAW_FEATURES)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Target distribution: {train['target'].value_counts().to_dict()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "feature-engineering",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Feature engineering function\n",
    "def add_features(df, feature_set='full'):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Add engineered features based on feature_set.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        feature_set: 'raw', 'expert', 'target', or 'full'\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    df = df.copy()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if feature_set == 'raw':\n",
    "        return df\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Expert features (medical domain knowledge)\n",
    "    if feature_set in ['expert', 'target', 'full']:\n",
    "        df['Rate_Pressure_Product'] = df['BP'] * df['Max HR']\n",
    "        df['MaxHR_Rel_Age'] = df['Max HR'] / (220 - df['Age']).replace(0, 1)\n",
    "        df['HR_Deficit'] = (220 - df['Age']) - df['Max HR']\n",
    "        df['Electrical_Stress'] = df['ST depression'] * df['Slope of ST']\n",
    "        df['Cholesterol_per_Age'] = df['Cholesterol'] / df['Age'].replace(0, 1)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Target encoding features (not used in final model, but tested)\n",
    "    if feature_set in ['target', 'full']:\n",
    "        # Would add target encoding here, but skipping for simplicity\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Additional domain features\n",
    "    if feature_set == 'full':\n",
    "        df['BP_per_Age'] = df['BP'] / df['Age'].replace(0, 1)\n",
    "        df['Vessel_Thallium'] = df['Number of vessels fluro'] * df['Thallium']\n",
    "        df['Angina_ST'] = df['Exercise angina'] * df['ST depression']\n",
    "        df['ST_per_HR'] = df['ST depression'] / df['Max HR'].replace(0, 1)\n",
    "        df['Cardiac_Risk'] = (\n",
    "            (df['BP'] > 140).astype(int) + (df['Cholesterol'] > 240).astype(int) +\n",
    "            df['Sex'].astype(int) + (df['Age'] > 55).astype(int) + df['FBS over 120'].astype(int)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        df['Typical_Angina'] = (df['Chest pain type'] == 4).astype(int)\n",
    "        df['Thallium_Abnormal'] = (df['Thallium'] != 3).astype(int)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return df\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply feature engineering\n",
    "train_raw = train.copy()\n",
    "train_expert = add_features(train, 'expert')\n",
    "train_full = add_features(train, 'full')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Feature sets\n",
    "EXPERT_FEATURES = ['Rate_Pressure_Product', 'MaxHR_Rel_Age', 'HR_Deficit', \n",
    "                   'Electrical_Stress', 'Cholesterol_per_Age']\n",
    "DOMAIN_FEATURES = ['BP_per_Age', 'Vessel_Thallium', 'Angina_ST', 'ST_per_HR',\n",
    "                   'Cardiac_Risk', 'Typical_Angina', 'Thallium_Abnormal']\n",
    "ALL_ENGINEERED = EXPERT_FEATURES + DOMAIN_FEATURES\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFeature counts:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Raw: {len(RAW_FEATURES)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  + Expert: {len(RAW_FEATURES) + len(EXPERT_FEATURES)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  + Domain: {len(RAW_FEATURES) + len(ALL_ENGINEERED)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ablation-experiment",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🧪 Ablation Experiment: Adding Features Incrementally\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll train CatBoost models with different feature sets and compare OOF AUC scores:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Raw 13 features** (baseline)\n",
    "2. **+ 5 expert features** (medical domain knowledge)\n",
    "3. **+ 7 domain features** (additional interactions)\n",
    "\n",
    "This will show which feature groups contribute most to performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ablation-cv",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def train_and_evaluate(df, features, n_splits=5, seed=42):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Train CatBoost with given features and return OOF AUC.\"\"\"\n",
    "    X = df[features]\n",
    "    y = df['target']\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Determine categorical features\n",
    "    cat_features = [f for f in features if f in CATS]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 5-fold CV\n",
    "    skf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=n_splits, shuffle=True, random_state=seed)\n",
    "    oof_preds = np.zeros(len(df))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for fold, (train_idx, val_idx) in enumerate(skf.split(X, y)):\n",
    "        X_tr, X_va = X.iloc[train_idx], X.iloc[val_idx]\n",
    "        y_tr, y_va = y.iloc[train_idx], y.iloc[val_idx]\n",
    "        \n",
    "        model = CatBoostClassifier(\n",
    "            iterations=500,\n",
    "            learning_rate=0.05,\n",
    "            depth=6,\n",
    "            l2_leaf_reg=3,\n",
    "            cat_features=cat_features,\n",
    "            random_seed=seed,\n",
    "            verbose=0,\n",
    "            task_type='CPU'\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        model.fit(X_tr, y_tr, eval_set=(X_va, y_va), early_stopping_rounds=50, verbose=0)\n",
    "        oof_preds[val_idx] = model.predict_proba(X_va)[:, 1]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    oof_auc = roc_auc_score(y, oof_preds)\n",
    "    return oof_auc, oof_preds\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run ablation experiments\n",
    "print(\"Running ablation experiments...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ablation_results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Raw features\n",
    "print(\"[1/3] Training with raw 13 features...\")\n",
    "auc_raw, _ = train_and_evaluate(train_raw, RAW_FEATURES)\n",
    "ablation_results.append({'Feature Set': 'Raw 13 features', 'OOF AUC': auc_raw, 'Features': 13})\n",
    "print(f\"  OOF AUC: {auc_raw:.5f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Raw + Expert\n",
    "print(\"[2/3] Training with raw + expert features...\")\n",
    "auc_expert, _ = train_and_evaluate(train_expert, RAW_FEATURES + EXPERT_FEATURES)\n",
    "ablation_results.append({'Feature Set': '+ Expert features', 'OOF AUC': auc_expert, 'Features': 18})\n",
    "print(f\"  OOF AUC: {auc_expert:.5f} ({auc_expert - auc_raw:+.5f})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Raw + Expert + Domain\n",
    "print(\"[3/3] Training with all engineered features...\")\n",
    "auc_full, _ = train_and_evaluate(train_full, RAW_FEATURES + ALL_ENGINEERED)\n",
    "ablation_results.append({'Feature Set': '+ Domain features', 'OOF AUC': auc_full, 'Features': 25})\n",
    "print(f\"  OOF AUC: {auc_full:.5f} ({auc_full - auc_raw:+.5f})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ablation_df = pd.DataFrame(ablation_results)\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(ablation_df.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ablation-viz",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize ablation results\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# OOF AUC progression\n",
    "ax = axes[0]\n",
    "colors = ['#3498db', '#e74c3c', '#2ecc71']\n",
    "bars = ax.bar(range(len(ablation_df)), ablation_df['OOF AUC'], color=colors, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(range(len(ablation_df)))\n",
    "ax.set_xticklabels(ablation_df['Feature Set'])\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('OOF AUC', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Ablation Study: Feature Set Performance', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_ylim(0.954, 0.956)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add value labels\n",
    "for i, row in ablation_df.iterrows():\n",
    "    ax.text(i, row['OOF AUC'] + 0.00005, f\"{row['OOF AUC']:.5f}\", ha='center', fontsize=11)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Delta from baseline\n",
    "ax = axes[1]\n",
    "baseline = ablation_df.iloc[0]['OOF AUC']\n",
    "deltas = (ablation_df['OOF AUC'] - baseline) * 1000\n",
    "colors_delta = ['#95a5a6', '#e74c3c', '#2ecc71']\n",
    "bars = ax.bar(range(len(ablation_df)), deltas, color=colors_delta, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(range(len(ablation_df)))\n",
    "ax.set_xticklabels(ablation_df['Feature Set'])\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Δ OOF AUC (×1000)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Change from Baseline (Raw 13)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.axhline(y=0, color='black', linestyle='-', linewidth=0.8)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add value labels\n",
    "for i, delta in enumerate(deltas):\n",
    "    y_pos = delta + 0.05 if delta > 0 else delta - 0.05\n",
    "    ax.text(i, y_pos, f\"{delta:+.2f}\", ha='center', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n🔍 Key Findings:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Expert features: {(auc_expert - auc_raw) * 1000:+.2f} (×1000)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Domain features: {(auc_full - auc_expert) * 1000:+.2f} (×1000)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total gain: {(auc_full - auc_raw) * 1000:+.2f} (×1000)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "shap-analysis",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📊 SHAP Feature Importance Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's use SHAP to understand which features are most important for the model's predictions.\n",
    "\n",
    "SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) provides:\n",
    "- Global feature importance (which features matter most)\n",
    "- Direction of impact (positive/negative contribution)\n",
    "- Individual prediction explanations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "train-full-model",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train a single model on all data for SHAP analysis\n",
    "print(\"Training final model for SHAP analysis...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "X_full = train_full[RAW_FEATURES + ALL_ENGINEERED]\n",
    "y_full = train_full['target']\n",
    "cat_features_full = [f for f in (RAW_FEATURES + ALL_ENGINEERED) if f in CATS]\n",
    "\n",
    "model_full = CatBoostClassifier(\n",
    "    iterations=500,\n",
    "    learning_rate=0.05,\n",
    "    depth=6,\n",
    "    l2_leaf_reg=3,\n",
    "    cat_features=cat_features_full,\n",
    "    random_seed=42,\n",
    "    verbose=0,\n",
    "    task_type='CPU'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_full.fit(X_full, y_full, verbose=0)\n",
    "print(\"✅ Model trained successfully\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create SHAP explainer\n",
    "print(\"\\nCreating SHAP explainer (this may take a minute)...\")\n",
    "explainer = shap.TreeExplainer(model_full)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sample data for SHAP (use 10000 samples for speed)\n",
    "sample_idx = np.random.choice(len(X_full), size=min(10000, len(X_full)), replace=False)\n",
    "X_sample = X_full.iloc[sample_idx]\n",
    "\n",
    "shap_values = explainer.shap_values(X_sample)\n",
    "print(\"✅ SHAP values computed\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "shap-summary",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# SHAP summary plot\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
    "shap.summary_plot(shap_values, X_sample, show=False, max_display=20)\n",
    "plt.title('SHAP Feature Importance: Global Impact', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', pad=20)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n📊 Interpretation:\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Features ranked by average absolute SHAP value\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Red: High feature value\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Blue: Low feature value\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Right side: Increases heart disease probability\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Left side: Decreases heart disease probability\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "shap-bar",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# SHAP bar plot (mean absolute importance)\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
    "shap.summary_plot(shap_values, X_sample, plot_type='bar', show=False, max_display=20)\n",
    "plt.title('SHAP Feature Importance: Mean Absolute Impact', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', pad=20)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "feature-importance-ranking",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate mean absolute SHAP values\n",
    "shap_importance = np.abs(shap_values).mean(axis=0)\n",
    "feature_importance = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'Feature': X_sample.columns,\n",
    "    'SHAP Importance': shap_importance\n",
    "}).sort_values('SHAP Importance', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mark engineered features\n",
    "feature_importance['Type'] = feature_importance['Feature'].apply(\n",
    "    lambda x: 'Engineered' if x in ALL_ENGINEERED else 'Raw'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n🏆 Top 15 Most Important Features:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
    "print(feature_importance.head(15).to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Count engineered features in top N\n",
    "top5_eng = feature_importance.head(5)['Type'].value_counts().get('Engineered', 0)\n",
    "top10_eng = feature_importance.head(10)['Type'].value_counts().get('Engineered', 0)\n",
    "top15_eng = feature_importance.head(15)['Type'].value_counts().get('Engineered', 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📈 Engineered features in top rankings:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Top 5: {top5_eng}/5 ({top5_eng/5*100:.0f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Top 10: {top10_eng}/10 ({top10_eng/10*100:.0f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Top 15: {top15_eng}/15 ({top15_eng/15*100:.0f}%)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "correlation-analysis",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔗 Feature Correlation Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's examine correlations between raw and engineered features to understand if:\n",
    "- Engineered features are redundant with raw features\n",
    "- Engineered features capture new information"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "correlation-heatmap",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Select top features for correlation analysis\n",
    "top_features = feature_importance.head(15)['Feature'].tolist()\n",
    "corr_matrix = train_full[top_features].corr()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot correlation heatmap\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 12))\n",
