    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"\\n✅ No highly correlated feature pairs (|r| > 0.7) among top features\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "paradox",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🤔 The Feature Engineering Paradox\n",
    "\n",
    "**Observed Results:**\n",
    "- OOF: Raw features better than engineered features\n",
    "- LB: Engineered features better than raw features (+0.00031)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hypothesis:** Engineered features act as **regularization**:\n",
    "1. Add controlled noise to training (hurts OOF)\n",
    "2. Force model to learn more robust patterns\n",
    "3. Improve generalization to test set (helps LB)\n",
    "\n",
    "This is similar to dropout in neural networks—it hurts training performance but improves test performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "paradox-viz",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the paradox\n",
    "paradox_data = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {'Metric': 'OOF AUC', 'Raw Features': 0.95537, 'Engineered Features': 0.95549, 'Delta': +0.00012},\n",
    "    {'Metric': 'LB AUC', 'Raw Features': 0.95341, 'Engineered Features': 0.95372, 'Delta': +0.00031},\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Side-by-side comparison\n",
    "ax = axes[0]\n",
    "x = np.arange(len(paradox_data))\n",
    "width = 0.35\n",
    "ax.bar(x - width/2, paradox_data['Raw Features'], width, label='Raw Features (13)', color='#3498db', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax.bar(x + width/2, paradox_data['Engineered Features'], width, label='Engineered (25)', color='#2ecc71', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(x)\n",
    "ax.set_xticklabels(paradox_data['Metric'])\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('AUC Score', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
